1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Step 1 - Open the TaaS Studio reviewer notebook on Google Colab

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Step 2 - Connect a free Colab runtime (CPU is enough, no GPU needed)

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Step 3 - Runtime connected - Colab clones the pinned TaaS revision

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Step 4 - Run all: checkout, install dependencies, start demo MCP server

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Step 5 - Cells run top-to-bottom - health and readiness checks pass

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Step 6 - Open Studio cell - Colab proxyPort generates the HTTPS Studio URL

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Step 7 - Studio is live - copy the ephemeral token and press Connect

8
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,190
1/8  Connect — open Studio, paste the API token, click Connect

9
00:00:55,190 --> 00:01:00,050
2/8  Overview — live runtime diagnostics and platform inventory

10
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:07,400
3/8  DEFINE — GoalSpec designer: templates are drafts, not validation

11
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:15,250
4/8  BUILD — Agent lifecycle: draft, validate, publish, sign, revoke

12
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:23,550
5/8  DISCOVER — MCP connections: tools/list inspection, never tools/call

13
00:01:23,550 --> 00:01:28,370
6/8  DISCOVER — Tool registry & persisted discovery history

14
00:01:28,370 --> 00:01:35,270
7/8  VERIFY — Audit timeline: load events, verify the hash chain

15
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:47,806
8/8  OPERATE & MANAGE — runtime diagnostics; unsupported data says UNAVAILABLE

